aecaf8bc4d446616d738d"],"m":1560},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1561","t":"Ifmyante wrote:\n\nabhishek512 wrote: Hi, I am wondering what made this 5min swap zone push price down to such an extent, as it was created and innored and after a while it just became dormant, but then all of a sudden last night it became active.. am i missing something here?\n\nhere is the approach:\n\nThank you for your valuable feedback IF... will go look for clues on the left.. this is zinc commodity futures chart from MCX india.\n\nlooks like its a zone where some good price action has occured in the past. price engulfed it both ways in past. can't say its a caps doubt anymore i guess.. will look further into it. here is the chart on further left\n\nregards, Abhi","a":"abhishek512","d":"","n":"#1561","p":63,"im":["5cfa6792f5bf605bcb63f422bb9c07aa661ddc5d","4e89f73472a25373f7aaecaf8bc4d446616d738d","600303cc7cbffba8b42bf4e3ab5c4db481a76ea1","2102816550b23a29e2166f7649574ac0bbf76ca9"],"m":1561},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1562","t":"Was drawing DBR and RBD on EURUSD Monthly chart and at some point I have no idea what i am drawing anymore...","a":"dengaima","d":"","n":"#1562","p":63,"im":["e89869ae8a892664ec3c1ea8e292e302b3602411"],"m":1562},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1563","t":"Dengaima, you should try marking DBR and RBD only. Don't mark FLs in the HW and definitely only mark the cleanest examples.","a":"Rinehart","d":"","n":"#1563","p":63,"im":["30c2b029195b6ac271760a807b73ad5df4fde80a"],"m":1563},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1564","t":"Rinehart wrote: Dengaima, you should try marking DBR and RBD only. Don't mark FLs in the HW and definitely only mark the cleanest examples.\n\nRinehart, how do you define good RBD/DBRs?\n\nAlso I have some questions on the chart below","a":"dengaima","d":"","n":"#1564","p":63,"im":["30c2b029195b6ac271760a807b73ad5df4fde80a","11355a6267a0e881b8e733fd94a8dc27e67407f8"],"m":1564},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1565","t":"Rinehart, is this better?\n\nOr maybe this is the way?=)","a":"dengaima","d":"","n":"#1565","p":63,"im":["3f7f3a21c7f7745c55144707ad8be4047092ad81","ff8c3bd1f201f97d2876b0ee810cbf2c13e218ce","4fefc411f7f758468d8b6b8d5082ac503b54a6a0"],"m":1565},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1566","t":"That's much better. A lot has been omitted, sure, but this view should serve its purpose: to show you how caps are respected, and give you an insight into what happens when they're not","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#1566","p":63,"im":[],"m":1566},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1567","t":"I have resumed to do my homeworks for marking the caps. I have used the higher time frame to clearly identify the caps. Master IF did say that nearly all the caps are tradable, but going through most of the homework’s I have marked most of the caps which are formed by braking or engulfing the previous low/high. Those set of caps have given a good reaction. The first set of them are been marked on the higher timeframes. Appreciate if you could validate them. Thank you!","a":"Mandrikan","d":"","n":"#1567","p":63,"im":["8af094c9613f321442f3f50f83f75299bbe15df9","b6c8b5bf0eae56116628af37bac11cd5a8100215","f4e333376df2739904bd56869324bd93df65d1ea"],"m":1567},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1568","t":"D -> Demand S --> Supply\n\nBlue Arrow it is to represent a reaction to the zone the Red arrow a failure","a":"Mandrikan","d":"","n":"#1568","p":63,"im":["62736fc825fb2bb09bdc0126310285be645ce2b0","c6f93b76bd48d3f2c53b0193d27abab1625732f2","6c01a57492e31c064c1969849374e02e3ced99da"],"m":1568},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1569","t":"Next I will start marking them on the lower timeframe.","a":"Mandrikan","d":"","n":"#1569","p":63,"im":["c7070c81e229e47cada095cd42c6449e0bcfd02b","bf6c8c7758140af4d7a64481052d742e8ef9b80e","c124f06090305daa4cc2c2f9596c6b5d30c7f3f1","37f363dc589a721258a32fdc17755488db083266"],"m":1569},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1570","t":"That's really good work!\n\nOnce you're finished with that, dive in again, looking for the left shoulders of caps, and you'll make a big leap","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#1570","p":63,"im":[],"m":1570},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1571","t":"Ifmyante, I got a question. From this chart that post, where the move is going first? I know that eventually they will hunt those stoplosses from top range, but they need bulls to move the price up there right? Therefore do they move price down first to fill up remaining buy orders then hunt stoplosses above?\n\nThe point is the engulf lower happened first, so price should retrace up before moving back down right? But if that's the case, then its possible for them to go straight for stop hunt and push price down to demand.\n\nI am quite confused after pondering for a while:D\n\nWell anyway its a daily chart so might take a year before what I said happens:D","a":"dengaima","d":"","n":"#1571","p":63,"im":["901741cf1b02999b5939ef89c230b184fdce6127"],"m":1571},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1572","t":"this right here, is a whole article about \"Supply & Demand\" (in which price caps are the essence of) summed up in 1 paragraph. kudos to you, IF","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1572","p":63,"im":["440d610a45970d665346aceb1c383d9a2d4a1d3a"],"m":1572},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1573","t":"It kind of is that simple, yes\n\nDengaima, be careful","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#1573","p":63,"im":["7b208fcfc1d2a9fe094c5ca54a518ece9d994d8f"],"m":1573},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1574","t":"Ifmyante wrote: It kind of is that simple, yes\n\nDengaima, be careful\n\nHow would you mark the chart then if there's a gap? Where would the DP be around the GAP area?","a":"dengaima","d":"","n":"#1574","p":63,"im":["7b208fcfc1d2a9fe094c5ca54a518ece9d994d8f"],"m":1574},{"id":"dbrrbd_p63_1575","t":"Hi all, Here is my RBD homework:\n\n57585960616263646566","a":"traderscape","d":"","n":"#1575","p":63,"im":["517cecc328616dcae0771a85090f769797790687","8f382eb48b332dcc0416328bd6a68417eca8065e","a15d251ca07142f9aa071419debcf92cb1f3c598","9e30d93ca5794af85373674e0a300fa9612be5dc","66cc9537c20677b8b59674d6b731ed7f7877fef3"],"m":1575}],"images":[{"k":"5cfa6792f5bf605bcb63f422bb9c07aa661ddc5d","t":"assets/thumbs/5cfa6792f5bf